<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<bpmn:definitions xmlns:bpmn="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/MODEL"
                  xmlns:bpmndi="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/DI"
                  xmlns:dc="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DC"
                  xmlns:di="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DI"
                  xmlns:operaton="http://operaton.org/schema/1.0/bpmn"
                  id="definitions" targetNamespace="http://bpmn.io/schema/bpmn">
  <bpmn:process id="scout_and_clone" name="Scout and clone" isExecutable="true" operaton:historyTimeToLive="180">
    <bpmn:documentation>The scout reads the prompt, the Vault and the Source map, never code, and names the repos, taking the start form's as given; Clone repos clones them on the work branch: the start form's branch, else the scout's. Needs start-form fields prompt, branch and repos.</bpmn:documentation>
    <bpmn:startEvent id="start">
      <bpmn:outgoing>f1</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:startEvent>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="scout" name="Scout" operaton:type="external" operaton:topic="agent">
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <operaton:properties>
          <operaton:property name="ants.agent" value="a-lead" />
          <operaton:property name="ants.name.a-lead" value="lead" />
          <operaton:property name="ants.level" value="2" />
          <operaton:property name="ants.assignment" value="Work out what the Run is about and which repos it needs, before anyone reads code. The Tasks after you clone the repos you name and read your brief.&#10;&#10;Your inputs:&#10;- `prompt`: what the user wants, in their words.&#10;- `sourceMap`: the repos the user has, `[{name, remote}]`.&#10;- `repos`: the repos the user picked on the start form, as they picked them (Source map names, git URLs, `owner/name` for a new repo); empty when they picked none.&#10;&#10;You read the prompt, the Source map and the Vault, and never code: there are no clones yet, and you must not look for any. You write only in `scout/`.&#10;&#10;1. Search the Vault. With no Vault named above, skip this step: the brief rests on the prompt alone. Load the search-knowledge Skill, then start the `knowledge-searcher` Subagent with the Vault's path, that Skill's folder and the subject of the prompt: the features, screens, services and terms it names, and which repos the Notes say hold them. Search once more if its answer opens a question the prompt depends on, or doesn't yet tie the work to a repo.&#10;&#10;2. Pick the repos. When `repos` holds any, the user picked them: take them as given. Don't add any, drop any or question them, a new repo or one outside the Source map included. Answer with `repos` exactly as you got them, and say in the brief what needs doing in each.&#10;Else you pick the repos the work changes, from the Source map: each Source map `name` the prompt names, matched loosely (case, spaces, hyphens, a plural, a common short form), and each git URL that appears word for word in the prompt; else each Source map `name` the Vault ties the work to: the repo a Note says holds the feature, screen or service the prompt is about, and the one the change has to be made in, not every repo the Notes mention. The repos you pick are only Source map names and the prompt's git URLs: never a repo outside the Source map, and never a new one.&#10;Answer `stuck` when you can't pick, and say in `needs` what you couldn't place and the Source map names closest to it, so the user can answer with the repos, then Continue: a repo the prompt names that matches no Source map name, or more than one; work the Vault ties to no repo, or to several with nothing to choose between them.&#10;&#10;3. Name a work branch: a short name for the work, such as `add-hello-endpoint`: lowercase, hyphens, no spaces. The user's own branch, given on the start form, wins over yours.&#10;&#10;4. Write `scout/brief.md`:&#10;- **Prompt**: the prompt as you understood it, in a few lines.&#10;- **Repos**: each repo in `repos` and what needs doing in it; for one you picked, the prompt's words or the `[[Note]]` that tie it to the work.&#10;- **Notes**: the relevant Vault Notes as `[[Name]]`, one line each on what they say.&#10;- **Open**: what the Vault doesn't answer that the work will need, and each repo the work may need that you didn't pick, with what would show it is needed. It is cloned only if the griller names it, so never call it unlikely to need a change.&#10;&#10;Answer `done` with `repos`, `branch` and `brief: &quot;scout/brief.md&quot;`." />
          <operaton:property name="ants.skills" value="k-search-knowledge" />
          <operaton:property name="ants.name.k-search-knowledge" value="search-knowledge" />
          <operaton:property name="ants.vault" value="true" />
          <operaton:property name="ants.result-schema" value="{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;object&quot;,&quot;properties&quot;:{&quot;repos&quot;:{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;array&quot;,&quot;items&quot;:{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;string&quot;,&quot;format&quot;:&quot;repo&quot;},&quot;description&quot;:&quot;The repos the user picked, exactly as given; else the ones the scout picks: Source map names, or git URLs word for word from the prompt.&quot;},&quot;branch&quot;:{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;string&quot;,&quot;description&quot;:&quot;A suggested work branch, such as add-hello-endpoint.&quot;},&quot;brief&quot;:{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;string&quot;,&quot;format&quot;:&quot;path&quot;,&quot;description&quot;:&quot;The brief, scout/brief.md.&quot;}},&quot;required&quot;:[&quot;repos&quot;,&quot;branch&quot;,&quot;brief&quot;],&quot;additionalProperties&quot;:false}" />
        </operaton:properties>
        <operaton:inputOutput>
          <operaton:inputParameter name="prompt">${prompt}</operaton:inputParameter>
          <operaton:inputParameter name="sourceMap">${sourceMap}</operaton:inputParameter>
          <operaton:inputParameter name="repos">${repos}</operaton:inputParameter>
        </operaton:inputOutput>
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>f1</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>f2</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="clone" name="Clone repos" operaton:type="external" operaton:topic="clone-repos">
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <operaton:inputOutput>
          <operaton:inputParameter name="repos">${scout.output.repos}</operaton:inputParameter>
          <operaton:inputParameter name="branch">${not empty branch ? branch : scout.output.branch}</operaton:inputParameter>
        </operaton:inputOutput>
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>f2</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>f3</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="end">
      <bpmn:incoming>f3</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="f1" sourceRef="start" targetRef="scout" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="f2" sourceRef="scout" targetRef="clone" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="f3" sourceRef="clone" targetRef="end" />
  </bpmn:process>
  <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="diagram">
    <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="plane" bpmnElement="scout_and_clone">
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="start_di" bpmnElement="start">
        <dc:Bounds x="180" y="160" width="36" height="36" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="scout_di" bpmnElement="scout">
        <dc:Bounds x="270" y="138" width="100" height="80" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="clone_di" bpmnElement="clone">
        <dc:Bounds x="420" y="138" width="100" height="80" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="end_di" bpmnElement="end">
        <dc:Bounds x="572" y="160" width="36" height="36" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="f1_di" bpmnElement="f1">
        <di:waypoint x="216" y="178" />
        <di:waypoint x="270" y="178" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="f2_di" bpmnElement="f2">
        <di:waypoint x="370" y="178" />
        <di:waypoint x="420" y="178" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="f3_di" bpmnElement="f3">
        <di:waypoint x="520" y="178" />
        <di:waypoint x="572" y="178" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
    </bpmndi:BPMNPlane>
  </bpmndi:BPMNDiagram>
</bpmn:definitions>
